{"cuisine/ancient-maya-cuisine":{"t":"cuisine","r":"cuisine/ancient-maya-cuisine","n":"Ancient Maya cuisine","c":"#94bd5c","crumb":[["The Americas","cuisines#the-americas"],["Mesoamerican cuisine","cuisine/mesoamerican-cuisine"]],"sub":"Regional cuisine in Mexico","intro":[["Today, ",["Maya families","cuisine/maya-cuisine"]," in Yucatán and Guatemala still farm the milpa and cook in earth ovens."]],"src":"note","sources":[{"name":"ECOSUR, Contemporary Maya food system in the lowlands of northern Yucatán","url":"https://sidalc.net/search/Record/KOHA-OAI-ECOSUR:6940"},{"name":"Uno TV, El pib, la tradición yucateca que se cocina bajo tierra","url":"https://www.unotv.com/estados/yucatan/el-pib-la-tradicion-yucateca-que-se-cocina-bajo-tierra/"}],"actions":[{"kind":"globe","hash":"ancient-maya-cuisine"},{"kind":"wiki","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ancient_Maya_cuisine"}],"sections":[{"h":"Recipe sites","empty":"None yet","tryLinks":[["Mesoamerican cuisine","cuisine/mesoamerican-cuisine"]]},{"h":"Part of","links":[["Mesoamerican cuisine","cuisine/mesoamerican-cuisine"]]}],"cont":"Cuisine of the Americas","img":{"src":"/world-cuisine/img/thumb/1/17/Tamal_colado._Mayan_food.jpg/500px-Tamal_colado._Mayan_food.jpg","w":500,"h":667,"by":"AraVazquez","lic":"CC BY-SA 4.0","licUrl":"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0","page":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Tamal_colado._Mayan_food.jpg"}},"ingredient/cuttlefish":{"t":"ingredient","r":"ingredient/cuttlefish","n":"Cuttlefish","c":"#c9b8dd","crumb":[["Ingredients","ingredients"]],"sub":"Ingredient in 3 dishes across 5 cuisines","intro":[["Cuttlefish, or cuttles, are marine molluscs of the family Sepiidae. They belong to the class Cephalopoda which also includes squid, octopuses, and nautiluses. Cuttlefish have a unique internal shell, the cuttlebone, which is used for control of buoyancy. They have large, W-shaped pupils, eight arms, and two tentacles furnished with denticulated suckers, with which they secure their prey. They generally range in size from 15 to 25 cm (6 to 10 in), with the largest species, the giant cuttlefish (Sepia apama), reaching 50 cm (20 in) in mantle length and more than 10.5 kg (23 lb) in mass."]],"src":"wikipedia","actions":[{"kind":"globe","hash":"ingredient-cuttlefish"},{"kind":"wiki","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Cuttlefish"}],"sections":[{"h":"Where it's cooked with","count":5,"groups":[["Andorran cuisine","cuisine/andorran-cuisine",[["Arròs negre","dish/arros-negre"]]],["Catalan cuisine","cuisine/catalan-cuisine",[["Arròs negre","dish/arros-negre"]]],["Chinese cuisine","cuisine/chinese-cuisine",[["Orange cuttlefish","dish/orange-cuttlefish"]]],["Korean Chinese cuisine","cuisine/korean-chinese-cuisine",[["Ulmyeon","dish/ulmyeon"]]],["Valencian cuisine","cuisine/valencian-cuisine",[["Arròs negre","dish/arros-negre"]]]]},{"h":"Often cooked with","links":[["Squid as food","ingredient/squid-as-food"],["Cephalopod ink","ingredient/cephalopod-ink"],["Cubanelle","ingredient/cubanelle"],["Rice","ingredient/rice"],["Sepiida","ingredient/sepiida"],["Agaricus bisporus","ingredient/agaricus-bisporus"],["Broth","ingredient/broth"],["Carrot","ingredient/carrot"],["Cornstarch","ingredient/cornstarch"],["Egg","ingredient/egg"],["Noodle","ingredient/noodle"],["Noodles","ingredient/noodles"],["Sea cucumber","ingredient/sea-cucumber"],["Shiitake","ingredient/shiitake"],["Shrimp","ingredient/shrimp"]]}],"img":{"src":"/world-cuisine/img/thumb/6/65/Sepia_com%C3%BAn_%28Sepia_officinalis%29%2C_Parque_natural_de_la_Arr%C3%A1bida%2C_Portugal%2C_2020-07-21%2C_DD_62.jpg/500px-Sepia_com%C3%BAn_%28Sepia_officinalis%29%2C_Parque_natural_de_la_Arr%C3%A1bida%2C_Portugal%2C_2020-07-21%2C_DD_62.jpg","w":500,"h":333,"by":"Diego Delso","lic":"CC BY-SA 4.0","licUrl":"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0","page":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Sepia_com%C3%BAn_(Sepia_officinalis)%2C_Parque_natural_de_la_Arr%C3%A1bida%2C_Portugal%2C_2020-07-21%2C_DD_62.jpg"}},"dish/chimichanga":{"t":"dish","r":"dish/chimichanga","n":"Chimichanga","c":"#ede6da","crumb":[["Dishes","dishes"]],"sub":"Dish found in 2 cuisines","dot":"#94bd5c","intro":[["A chimichanga is a deep-fried burrito that is common in Southwestern U.S. cuisine. The dish is typically prepared by filling a flour tortilla with various ingredients, most commonly rice, cheese, beans, and a meat, such as machaca (chopped or shredded meat), carne adobada (marinated meat), carne seca (dried beef), or shredded chicken, and folding it into a rectangular package. It is then deep-fried, and can be accompanied by salsa, guacamole, or sour cream."]],"src":"wikipedia","actions":[{"kind":"globe","hash":"dish-chimichanga"},{"kind":"wiki","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Chimichanga"}],"sections":[{"h":"Where it's from","links":[["American cuisine","cuisine/american-cuisine"],["Mexican cuisine","cuisine/mexican-cuisine"]]},{"h":"Ingredients","count":9,"links":[["Adobada","ingredient/adobada"],["Bean","ingredient/bean"],["Cheese","ingredient/cheese"],["Chicken","ingredient/chicken"],["Flour tortilla","ingredient/flour-tortilla"],["Jalapeño","ingredient/jalapeno"],["Machaca","ingredient/machaca"],["Rice","ingredient/rice"],["Tortilla","ingredient/tortilla"]]},{"h":"Cook it","rows":[{"name":"Mexico in My Kitchen","color":"#55b8ad","shape":"site","sub":"mexicoinmykitchen.com","note":"Mely Martínez's long-running blog of Mexican home-style recipes.","url":"https://www.mexicoinmykitchen.com/","suggested":true,"kind":"blog"},{"name":"Pati Jinich","color":"#55b8ad","shape":"site","sub":"patijinich.com","note":"Recipe archive from the Mexican-born chef and host of the PBS series Pati's Mexican Table.","url":"https://patijinich.com/recipes/","suggested":true,"kind":"site"}]},{"h":"More from American cuisine","links":[["Angel food cake","dish/angel-food-cake"],["Banana bread","dish/banana-bread"],["Banana pudding","dish/banana-pudding"],["Barbecue sauce","dish/barbecue-sauce"],["Beer c